Reason (R): They block cold Siberian continental winds from entering India in winter and trap monsoon rain-bearing winds.', '{"A":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A","B":"Both A and R are true but R is NOT correct explanation of A","C":"A is true but R is false","D":"A is false but R is true"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'Social Science', 'Climate', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The sheer altitude and continuous chain of the Himalayas shield northern India from Arctic cold blasts while forcing monsoon moisture to precipitate over the plains.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000013', 'Assertion (A): Democracy is regarded as the most preferred form of government across the modern world.
Reason (R): Democratic governments are more accountable to the people and allow room for correcting mistakes through consultation.', '{"A":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A","B":"Both A and R are true but R is NOT correct explanation of A","C":"A is true but R is false","D":"A is false but R is true"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'ASSERTION_REASON', 'Social Science', 'What is Democracy? Why Democracy?', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Democracy improves decision-making quality through debate, accommodates diverse social groups, and provides constitutional mechanisms to peacefully correct errors.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000014', 'On 14th July 1789, the agitated people of Paris stormed which fortress prison, symbolizing royal despotism?', '{"A":"Bastille","B":"Tuileries","C":"Versailles","D":"Louvre"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'ASSERTION_REASON', 'Social Science', 'The French Revolution', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The storming of the Bastille on July 14, 1789, marked the dramatic outbreak of the French Revolution against Louis XVI''s autocratic rule.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000015', 'Distinguish between Western Ghats and Eastern Ghats on the basis of: (i) Continuity, (ii) Average elevation.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'Physical Features of India', 2, '(i) Continuity: Western Ghats are continuous and can be crossed only through passes (Thal, Bhor, and Pal Ghats), whereas Eastern Ghats are discontinuous and dissected by east-flowing rivers. (ii) Elevation: Western Ghats have higher average elevation (900-1600 m); Eastern Ghats have lower elevation (~600 m).', '1 Mark for continuity comparison; 1 Mark for elevation comparison', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000016', 'What is meant by ''disguised unemployment''? Give a real-life example from the rural agricultural sector.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'People as Resource', 2, 'Disguised unemployment occurs when more people are employed in an activity than actually required. Even if extra workers are withdrawn, total output does not diminish. Example: A rural family of 8 working on a 2-hectare plot where only 5 are needed; the remaining 3 are disguisedly unemployed.', '1 Mark for definition of disguised unemployment; 1 Mark for valid agricultural farming illustration', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000017', 'What were the three estates in 18th-century French society? Which estate paid all the taxes?', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'The French Revolution', 2, 'The three estates were: First Estate (Clergy), Second Estate (Nobility), and Third Estate (Big businessmen, merchants, court officials, lawyers, peasants, and landless artisans). Only the Third Estate paid all direct and indirect taxes (Taille and Tithe).', '1 Mark for listing the 3 estates correctly; 1 Mark for specifying that the Third Estate bore all taxes', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000018', 'What is the ''Preamble'' to the Indian Constitution? State any two core democratic values enshrined in it.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Social Science', 'Constitutional Design', 2, 'The Preamble is an introductory guiding statement that sets out the guiding purposes, principles, and philosophy of the Constitution. Core values: Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic, Justice, Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity (any two).', '1 Mark for definition of Preamble; 1 Mark for mentioning two core values with brief context', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-000000000019', 'Explain the factors that control the climate of any region, known as the six major climatic controls.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Climate', 3, 'The six major climatic controls of any place are: 1. Latitude (distance from equator affecting solar radiation), 2. Altitude (decrease in temperature with elevation), 3. Pressure and wind system (determines precipitation and humidity), 4. Distance from the sea (continentality vs moderating maritime effect), 5. Ocean currents (warm or cold coastal currents), 6. Relief features (mountains acting as barriers to rain-bearing winds).', '0.5 Mark for each correctly explained climatic control (total 3 Marks)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-00000000001a', 'Explain any three major demands made by Vladimir Lenin in his famous ''April Theses'' of 1917.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Socialism in Europe and the Russian Revolution', 3, 'In April 1917, Bolshevik leader Vladimir Lenin returned to Russia and put forward three urgent demands known as April Theses: 1. The ongoing First World War must be brought to an immediate close. 2. All land owned by the nobility and clergy must be transferred to the peasants. 3. All banks must be nationalized under state control.', '1 Mark for end of World War I; 1 Mark for transfer of land to peasants; 1 Mark for nationalization of banks', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-00000000001b', 'Describe the three Himalayan river systems that form the northern plains of India and state two characteristics of their drainage.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Drainage', 3, 'The three river systems are: 1. The Indus River System, 2. The Ganga River System, 3. The Brahmaputra River System. Characteristics: (i) They are perennial rivers fed by both rainfall and melting Himalayan snow. (ii) In their upper courses, they perform intensive erosional action forming deep gorges, while in lower courses they create floodplains, meanders, and expansive deltas.', '1 Mark for naming the three river systems; 2 Marks for two distinct hydrological characteristics (perennial flow and depositional landforms)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90030007-0000-4000-8000-00000000001c', 'Why is an independent and impartial judiciary essential in a constitutional democracy like India?', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Social Science', 'Constitutional Design', 3, 'An independent judiciary is vital because: 1. Protector of Fundamental Rights: Citizens can approach courts (High Courts and Supreme Court) under Articles 32 and 226 if rights are infringed. 2. Guardian of the Constitution: It has the power of Judicial Review to strike down unconstitutional executive orders and parliamentary laws. 3. Dispute Resolution: It resolves legal disputes between center and states or between citizens and the state impartially.', '1 Mark for protection of Fundamental Rights; 1 Mark for Judicial Review; 1 Mark for federal dispute settlement', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
